00:05:10.190 --> 00:05:12.356
Thing of the Week, which
is a cool thing of the week

00:05:12.356 --> 00:05:14.920
because it means that
you're going to save money.

00:05:14.920 --> 00:05:19.030
You can attach local
Solid-State Disks, SSDs.

00:05:19.030 --> 00:05:22.630
So you can attach them to any
kind of Google Compute Engine

00:05:22.630 --> 00:05:23.710
instance.

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:25.990
And before it had
the same price,

00:05:25.990 --> 00:05:28.730
no matter what kind of instance
you were attaching it to.

00:05:28.730 --> 00:05:31.030
Now, whenever you're
attaching them

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:34.940
to either on-demand or
preemptible instances,

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:37.480
they will be way,
way, way cheaper.

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:39.250
To the point that if
you're attaching them

00:05:39.250 --> 00:05:44.620
to an on-demand instance,
it will be 63% less

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:46.270
than what it was before.

00:05:46.270 --> 00:05:50.230
And for preemptible instances,
it's 71% cheaper than before.

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:51.770
It is a huge discount.

00:05:51.770 --> 00:05:54.270
So if you're doing things
like running MapReduce

00:05:54.270 --> 00:05:58.270
of bad jobs, where you need
a lot of really fast storage,

00:05:58.270 --> 00:06:01.360
you can use local SSDs
with preemptible machines.

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:04.420
And it's going to be incredibly
affordable now, so yay.

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:06.120
MARK MANDEL: Yay,
price lower, good.

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:07.780
FRANCESC CAMPOY:
Yeah, I like it.

00:06:07.780 --> 00:06:08.319
It's simple.

00:06:08.319 --> 00:06:08.860
It's cheaper.

00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:09.545
Like it better.

00:06:09.545 --> 00:06:10.420
MARK MANDEL: Exactly.

00:06:10.420 --> 00:06:10.810
Wonderful.

00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:11.310
Awesome.

