00:32:19.740 --> 00:32:21.687
because you sent
a bunch of them.

00:32:21.687 --> 00:32:23.520
We decided to go with
the last one you sent,

00:32:23.520 --> 00:32:28.320
which is about is there a way to
access the Kubernetes dashboard

00:32:28.320 --> 00:32:30.600
without running kubectl proxy?

00:32:30.600 --> 00:32:32.620
And the context
is, for instance,

00:32:32.620 --> 00:32:34.380
if I wanted to do
something quickly

00:32:34.380 --> 00:32:36.280
on the road from a mobile phone.

00:32:36.280 --> 00:32:37.490
So what do you think?

00:32:37.490 --> 00:32:39.856
Is there a way to do this?

00:32:39.856 --> 00:32:41.730
MARK MANDEL: This is an
interesting question.

00:32:41.730 --> 00:32:46.000
I think the answer is kind
of no-ish, because reasons.

00:32:46.000 --> 00:32:47.580
So let's kind of
walk through them.

00:32:47.580 --> 00:32:50.779
So generally speaking, if
you want to access the UI--

00:32:50.779 --> 00:32:52.320
so if you're not
familiar, Kubernetes

00:32:52.320 --> 00:32:53.340
comes with a dashboard.

00:32:53.340 --> 00:32:55.890
It gives you visualization
of what Kubernetes is doing.

00:32:55.890 --> 00:32:58.320
But it also allows you
to sort of deploy stuff,

00:32:58.320 --> 00:33:01.350
edit stuff, basically administer
your whole cluster if you

00:33:01.350 --> 00:33:02.490
want to do it through UI.

00:33:02.490 --> 00:33:04.860
Generally speaking, you want
to use the kubectl proxy.

00:33:04.860 --> 00:33:06.610
Because that's going
to give you security.

00:33:06.610 --> 00:33:07.590
That's the secure way.

00:33:07.590 --> 00:33:09.340
You're going to log in
with your credentials.

00:33:09.340 --> 00:33:10.080
And that's all
going to be set up

00:33:10.080 --> 00:33:11.330
and work the way it should do.

00:33:11.330 --> 00:33:13.530
In previous versions or
depending on your setup

00:33:13.530 --> 00:33:16.140
for your Kubernetes proxy,
you could access the UI

00:33:16.140 --> 00:33:19.060
through the IP address
of your master.

00:33:19.060 --> 00:33:19.926
OK, it works.

00:33:19.926 --> 00:33:21.300
Generally, though,
I think you'll

00:33:21.300 --> 00:33:23.647
find on newer versions
of Kubernetes that

00:33:23.647 --> 00:33:25.230
weren't work nearly
as well or it just

00:33:25.230 --> 00:33:28.030
won't work at all because things
like RBAC and things like that.

00:33:28.030 --> 00:33:31.470
So you have policies that say
what you can access from where.

00:33:31.470 --> 00:33:33.810
I think that's probably a
good thing, because you really

00:33:33.810 --> 00:33:36.760
don't want like people from
outside of the world accessing

00:33:36.760 --> 00:33:37.260
your master.

00:33:37.260 --> 00:33:38.110
That's pretty bad.

00:33:38.110 --> 00:33:40.193
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Because
the dashboard is not only

00:33:40.193 --> 00:33:42.590
a dashboard in the
point of read only.

00:33:42.590 --> 00:33:44.310
You can actually
delete stuff, right?

00:33:44.310 --> 00:33:45.060
MARK MANDEL: Yeah.

00:33:45.060 --> 00:33:46.500
Yeah, you can delete pods.

00:33:46.500 --> 00:33:49.777
You can edit like your
YAML file configurations.

00:33:49.777 --> 00:33:52.110
Like, you could basically do
whatever you like in there.

00:33:52.110 --> 00:33:54.318
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Maybe even
access secrets, so, yeah.

00:33:54.318 --> 00:33:55.320
MARK MANDEL: Yeah.

00:33:55.320 --> 00:33:57.690
If you wanted to
access stuff or like

00:33:57.690 --> 00:34:00.840
see what was going on from
your phone, unfortunately,

00:34:00.840 --> 00:34:03.480
right now you don't have access
to Cloud Shell from your phone.

00:34:03.480 --> 00:34:06.350
But I would say you
could fire up a small VM,

00:34:06.350 --> 00:34:08.370
login SSH into that
from your phone,

00:34:08.370 --> 00:34:10.199
and run kubectl
commands, and still

00:34:10.199 --> 00:34:11.730
be able to see what's going on.

00:34:11.730 --> 00:34:12.855
FRANCESC CAMPOY: I checked.

00:34:12.855 --> 00:34:15.210
And indeed, the
Android application

00:34:15.210 --> 00:34:19.530
does not provide
a Cloud Shell yet.

00:34:19.530 --> 00:34:22.750
But I pinged a PM, being
like, dude, come on.

00:34:22.750 --> 00:34:23.481
[LAUGHTER]

00:34:23.481 --> 00:34:25.230
MARK MANDEL: I reckon
we should have that.

00:34:25.230 --> 00:34:25.889
That's my opinion.

00:34:25.889 --> 00:34:28.055
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Especially
because you can actually

00:34:28.055 --> 00:34:29.480
access it through the web.

00:34:29.480 --> 00:34:31.729
Like, you can actually visit
Console [INAUDIBLE] Cloud

00:34:31.729 --> 00:34:33.719
at google.com come
from your mobile phone

00:34:33.719 --> 00:34:36.060
and start Cloud
Shell from there.

00:34:36.060 --> 00:34:38.159
But there's some
problem there, too,

00:34:38.159 --> 00:34:40.170
and the typing does
not work that easily,

00:34:40.170 --> 00:34:43.081
which means that at the end of
the day, kind of hard to use.

00:34:43.081 --> 00:34:44.580
But the good thing
about Cloud Shell

00:34:44.580 --> 00:34:48.239
is that you can also
do the port preview.

00:34:48.239 --> 00:34:51.889
So you will be able to access,
as a web server, your Cloud

00:34:51.889 --> 00:34:53.250
Shell, right?

00:34:53.250 --> 00:34:54.780
And this is actually
totally secure,

00:34:54.780 --> 00:34:57.450
because only if you're
signed in with your account,

00:34:57.450 --> 00:34:59.430
you will be able to
access that port, which

00:34:59.430 --> 00:35:03.730
means that you will be
able to use kubectl proxy

00:35:03.730 --> 00:35:05.680
and access it securely.

00:35:05.680 --> 00:35:07.900
Because otherwise,
if you do it the way

00:35:07.900 --> 00:35:10.840
you were saying, if you
create a small instance

00:35:10.840 --> 00:35:13.480
and you SSH into it, which you
can do from the Android app,

00:35:13.480 --> 00:35:17.080
by the way, then the problem
is that then, yes, kubectl,

00:35:17.080 --> 00:35:18.190
whatever, will work.

00:35:18.190 --> 00:35:20.670
kubectl proxy will open a port.

00:35:20.670 --> 00:35:22.640
But then you need to
open it from the outset.

00:35:22.640 --> 00:35:23.960
And then anyone can access it.

00:35:23.960 --> 00:35:26.020
So we go back to the
problem that anyone

00:35:26.020 --> 00:35:29.570
could access your dashboard,
which is a really bad idea.

00:35:29.570 --> 00:35:31.524
So I guess the answer
is don't do it?

00:35:31.524 --> 00:35:33.190
MARK MANDEL: I would
say the answer then

00:35:33.190 --> 00:35:34.780
is just open your laptop.

00:35:34.780 --> 00:35:36.200
Use Cloud Shell to get in.

00:35:36.200 --> 00:35:37.120
Then you can still
do on the road.

00:35:37.120 --> 00:35:39.190
You don't need the tools
necessarily on that laptop.

00:35:39.190 --> 00:35:41.398
And then you can continue
to work forward from there.

00:35:41.398 --> 00:35:43.486
But I will say thanks so
much for this question.

00:35:43.486 --> 00:35:44.860
It actually spent
a bunch of time

00:35:44.860 --> 00:35:46.540
